{"title":"The Red Onion Font","link":"https://kottke.org/25/08/the-red-onion-font","date":1755121639000,"content":"\n        <p>The latest post from The Pudding starts off about as good as possible to attract the likes of me: “This is a project about onions and math.” I mean, yes. I’m in. And I enjoyed the interactive article, <a href=\"https://pudding.cool/2025/08/onions/\">Dicing an Onion the Mathematically Optimal Way</a>, but the design was absolutely delightful and onion-y:</p>\n\n<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/onion-font-01.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/onion-font-01.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/onion-font-01.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1194\" height=\"776\" alt=\"Dicing an Onion&lt;br /&gt;\nthe Mathematically Optimal Way where the letters of the word 'onion' look like sliced red onions\" /></p>\n\n<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/onion-font-02.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/onion-font-02.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/onion-font-02.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1124\" height=\"311\" alt=\"the letters of the word 'explore' look like sliced red onions\" /></p>\n\n<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/onion-font-03.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/onion-font-03.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/onion-font-03.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1225\" height=\"413\" alt=\"interface slider elements where the slider knobs look like sliced red onions\" /></p>\n\n<p>They even used an onion gradient for the border of the page. This must have been so fun to work on! Initially, I thought they’d designed the onion font, but a quick search turned up Handmadefont’s <a href=\"https://handmadefont.com/shop/oniotype-font/\">OnioType Font</a>:</p>\n\n<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/onion-font-04.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/onion-font-04.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/onion-font-04.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1184\" height=\"792\" alt=\"type sample ('the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog') where the letters look like sliced red onions\" /></p>\n\n<p>From the description, it sounds like the letterforms are made from real onions:</p>\n\n<blockquote><p>Each letter is lovingly crafted from a perfectly sliced red onion, where nature’s concentric rings do most of the design heavy-lifting. Vivid purples, tender whites, and sudden flashes of yellow form shapes so unexpectedly elegant, you’ll never look at a salad the same way again.</p></blockquote>\n\n<p>But I dunno…Photoshop might be a better guess. Still! I love this font and kudos to The Pudding for putting it to good use.</p>\n\n        \n\n         <p><strong>Tags:</strong> <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/cooking\">cooking</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/design\">design</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/food\">food</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/infoviz\">infoviz</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/mathematics\">mathematics</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/The%20Pudding\">The Pudding</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/typography\">typography</a></p>\n\n         <p>💬 <a href=\"https://kottke.org/25/08/the-red-onion-font\">Join the discussion on kottke.org</a> →</p>\n\n    ","author":"Jason Kottke","siteTitle":"Kottke","siteHash":"89a883271b4598f9b33ebe87be70d38557bcd266e68aee521a8f93622e0ab723","entryHash":"a4c1607bb2d8bbb015f90b64f297659a1b3eac35fb96f44a78bf939b7bad9700","category":"Sites"}